hello and welcome back to PlayStation  granade 10 years ago burnout paradise  hit the ps3 and the 360 to rave reviews  but it's never received the second  outing that it truly deserved so much  time has now passed that many new  players have never heard of Paradise  City but oh my word  the remaster is absolutely perfect and  I'll happily tell you why the awesome  speed and crash is the hidden game mode  the compelling online it's all here so  here are 7 ways burnout paradise  remastered is the perfect arcade racer  open worlds in racing games began with  Paradise City and the spectacle of  winding roads in the mountains and  densely populated intersections of the  city areas driving through each of those  junctions reveals an assignment if that  mission is not for you simply keep on  driving you are never forced to complete  any task in burnout paradise minder that  there are a hundred and twenty events  ready to launch from a hundred and  twenty different traffic signals around  the city so you're never more than a  moment from some burnout action should  you decide to take part in a race or any  other event for that matter slow down  and hold l2 and r2 at the lights the  core game modes are racing from A to B  against seven other drivers but going A  to B is only the starting point as you  must decide the best route to take it's  unbelievably easy to take a wrong turn  and turn a certain first-place finish  into a last-place mess up if you're not  one to go racing then go on time stunt  challenges instead flipping and smashing  your way around the city or what about  trying road rage in which you smash  other cars into walls and oncoming  vehicles there's even a marked man race  modifier where you are forced to reach a  destination without your car being  destroyed by other aggressive vehicles  victories in any or all of these  disciplines tie into the progression  system and the hunt for the sacred  burnouts license and when that's  achieved the real tests begin scratching  the surface of burnout paradise  remastered reveal so much more for  gamers to get their teeth into as new  vehicles are unlocked they aren't simply  placed in your garage like every other  racing game you've played know instead  that vehicle can be found racing  around the streets anywhere in the open  world if you really want that vehicle  you must take it down this small update  to accessing vehicles keeps you on your  toes as any second that roadster you've  always wanted  suddenly races by on into the distance  time to shut it down the Carson and  Bennett Grand Marais has been delivered  to your junkyard  now it's a wreck and it's yours going  back to the junkyard and taking that  wreckage to a trusty mechanic and now  the car is completely ready to go on the  open road speaking of cars there are 75  to unlock smash repair and drive but  that's only the beginning burnout  paradise remastered includes all eight  Adams from the original game this means  there are motorbikes remote-control cars  I'm not lying  Beach boogies and even the Ghostbusters  ride gets an outing in Paradise the  customization isn't fantastic but colors  and paint finishes can be selected and  can even be changed on the fly by going  through spray shops it can even be done  mid race every vehicle you unlock really  does feel like a reward and the stats  help us decide how the cash should be  used  is it a build for speed for stumps offer  taking down other players oh and look  the freakin DeLorean from Back to the  Future is here ea just take my money but  wait there's even more to uncover in  Paradise City burnouts approach to  collectibles is one of the most  addicting I've ever experienced spread  across the entire world are these yellow  do not enter signs which reveal hidden  shortcuts to give you the edge in races  suddenly a winding road can be  completely missed by searching for  hidden routes around the location the  collectibles don't end there as  billboards can be smashed and super  jumps can be found that resemble the  photo jumps back in the Tony Hawk's days  on top of this is our ability to rule  roads around the city and countryside  every single road has a time trial and a  crash mode to plunder every time you  drive across a road the time is recorded  even if you don't want to race at that  point a small 8 second road are a three  minute Road your time is always stored  and if you manage to beat the record the  street sign becomes silver to show you  that you hold a record here to make the  sign go golden you must take part in the  iconic crash mode  is famous for here in Paradise City this  is called Showtime Showtime is all about  causing as much damage as possible and  maneuvering your wreck into other cars  and buses for multipliers to start  Showtime press l1 and r1 together and  begin the carnage you can spend hundreds  of hours in paradise remastered  completely ignoring the main game and  instead owning every street you drive on  once you hold both speed and crush  record the street sign becomes gold  until somebody beats you of course we  must pause for a moment and take note of  the sublime soundtrack included in the  game it's such a focus that the our one  button is dedicated to switching tracks  if the current song doesn't suit your  mood mammoth bands like Faith No More  and Guns and Roses head up the  soundtrack and previous tombs in the  burnout series also make a return it may  be a soundtrack better suited to ten  years ago but for someone who played the  original this will make the feeling of  belonging and those nostalgia moments  come hopping back going online and  there's even more to uncover in burnout  paradise remastered by pressing right on  the d-pad we can hop onto online play  and race alongside seven randoms or  seven friends as it's an open world  there's nothing stopping anyone from  driving away and doing their own thing  but by teaming up there are further  challenges to perform in teams of two  three and so on and so forth for example  you and a buddy can race head-on over a  jump and crash midair to unlock one  challenge these are free roam or free  burn challenges and there's 352 master  plus another seventy time challenges ten  motorbike trials and ten island  challenges too from all the DLC we get  for free this game will take over your  life it's so packed with things to do so  in conclusion is burnout paradise  remastered worth returning to in my mind  oh my god yes it is of course there are  some shortcomings due to the era the  original was made controls and heads-up  displays have changed in particularly in  the last few years but in the last 10  years of searching for an arcade  open-world game I have never found one  that better to burn out paradise the  remaster is just as great as the  original with shiny new graphics  improved responsive 'ti and frame rates  and soup  online stability if this paved the way  for burnout paradise - then I'll be  absolutely ecstatic what do you think  about returning to games ten years later  and will you be venturing back into  paradise or maybe it's your first time  hearing about this title I'd love to  know your thoughts I'm Adam from  PlayStation granade and I'm going back  to practice my parallel parking it's  been a pleasure I'll see you next time  power parking the only way to park in  Paradise Hey Hey You you I don't like a  girlfriend no oh my god I'm singing  opera Levine what have you done to me  burn up
 

